# FIXED-BLOCKS-AUDIT, the expression text, slice 2 (Codex 2026-10-06): the value a reference takes is as long as
# the program writes it -- it went through a buffer of 1024 bytes and was refused "expression too long" past it.
# p is declared with c.strchr over a literal of 1500 bytes and 'xyz', q assigned the same: both point at the 'x'
# past the literal, so p[1] is 'y' (121) and q[2] 'z' (122).  A raw C call: native only.
fn: f () int
    @: char p c.strchr("", 120)
    @: char q 0
    q: c.strchr("", 120)
    if: p = 0 || q = 0
        return: 81
    int: v c.abs(p[1])
    int: z c.abs(q[2])
return: v + z - 236
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: f(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
